:''Not to be confused with [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]].''
'''Ensanglion the Calamity''' (超禍獣シングリオン, ''Chō Kajū Shingurion'', '''Super Calamity Beast Shinglion''') is a [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]]/[[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoth]] enemy introduced in the 20th stage of each [[Behemoth Culling]] map. He is an enemy counterpart of [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]. He was added in [[Version 12.7 Update|Version 12.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Ensanglion the Calamity
|image = E 659.png
|first appearance = [[Hidden Forest of Gapra]]
|money drop = 4,000¢ - 15,800¢
}}

==Enemy==
This fast, tough enemy stands at 350 range but slowly fires off ''highly'' devastating attacks that reach up to 550 range, weakening any survivors to 50%. Freeze, Slow, [[Wave Attack|Waves]] and [[Surge Attack|Surges]] all have no effect on him, and while vulnerable to Knockback effects, that does help in skipping his very short backswing. Combined with his low knockback count itself and any support in play, getting to this enemy may be easier said than done. His main weakness is that his attack animation's foreswing is quite long, meaning he isn't all that difficult to stall in the end as you can potentially interrupt the attack for a window of opportunity.

==Strategy==
[[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Yukimura]] and [[Awakened Bahamut Cat]] are able to do decent damage on him when timed well. [[Courier Cat]] and [[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]] can also do chip damage to him, as well as the peons in his debut stages. [[Radical Cat]] can also stall him well, but needs to be at least level 38 to survive a hit. [[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] is also a great choice against Ensanglion, since it can shrug off his 200,000 damage like nothing. Dodge units like [[Miku Cat (Rare Cat)|Miku Cat]] can be used in Metal Cat's absence, as they can do something similar with just a bit of luck. Keep in mind that unlike his [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|cat-counterpart]], he will '''immediately''' start moving once his attack animation is over and nothing gets in his way, and with the speed this flying beast has, it will reach your base like a breeze so stalling with good timing is necessary! Due to the lack of knockback immunity you can use breaker blast or [[Fortune Teller Cat (Rare Cat)|Fortune Teller Cat]] to interrupt his attack animation and grant your units to damage Ensanglion just for slightly longer.

