==Trivia==
*Ensanglion's name is a portmanteau of ''ensanguine'' (to stain or cover with blood) and ''[[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]]''.
*The "Shin" in Ensanglion's Japanese name (シングリオン ''Shingurion'', "Shinglion" or "Singlion"), could be derived from 死 ''shi'' (death), 神 ''shin'' (god), 身 ''shin'' (body), シン ''shin'' (sin, in reference to him being more sinful than Ganglion), or most likely 真 ''shin'' (true), contrasting Ganglion's name, where "Gan" can be taken as 贋 (counterfeit, fake).
*Ensanglion's miasma turning normal beasts into [[:Category:Behemoth Enemies|Behemoths]] is conceptually similar to the [[wikia:monsterhunter:Frenzy Virus|Frenzy Virus]] introduced in [[wikia:monsterhunter:Monster Hunter 4|''Monster Hunter 4'']], as both result in those afflicted gaining vastly increased strength, speed, savagery, aggression, and [[Casaurian Darkjo|red]] [[Cumulus Gallus|eyes]]. The Frenzy Virus is caused by [[wikia:monsterhunter:Gore Magala|Gore Magala]] and its adult stage, [[wikia:monsterhunter:Shagaru Magala|Shagaru Magala]], which acts as the "final boss" of ''Monster Hunter 4'', just as Ensanglion is the final boss of the [[Behemoth Culling]] maps. Shagaru Magala and most of ''Monster Hunter''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s other "final bosses" also happen to be [[wikia:monsterhunter:Elder Dragon|Elder Dragons]], like Ensanglion and Ganglion.
**Ensanglion's design has elements of Ganglion's Normal Form (color) and Evolved Form (wings), which is similar to how [[wikia:monsterhunter:Chaotic Gore Magala|Chaotic Gore Magala]] is stuck halfway between Gore Magala and Shagaru Magala.
**Ensanglion's Japanese description refers to him as an ancient/elder dragon (古龍 ''koryū''), while [[Pterowl Hazuku]]'s Japanese name (超竜獣オウルハズク'' Chō Ryūjū Ōruhazuku'') translates to "Super Dragon-Beast Owlhazuku", but they use different kanji for "dragon": Ensanglion's is 龍, whereas Hazuku's is 竜. In ''Monster Hunter'' terms, Ensanglion is an Elder Dragon (古龍種 ''Koryūshu''), but Hazuku is only a [[wikia:monsterhunter:Flying Wyvern|Flying Wyvern]] (飛竜種 ''Hiryūshu'') or [[wikia:monsterhunter:Bird Wyvern|Bird Wyvern]] (鳥竜種 ''Chōryūshu'').
*The word 分身 ''bunshin'' in Ensanglion's Japanese description can refer to a clone, alter-ego, or one of the bodies resulted from the split of another into multiple parts; an offshoot. Regardless of semantics, Ensanglion's virtuous other self would presumably be Ganglion.
**The duality of Ganglion and Ensanglion is similar to a pair of characters from ''Dragon Ball'': the good [[wikia:dragonball:Kami|Kami]] and the evil [[wikia:dragonball:King Piccolo|King Piccolo]], who were once a [[wikia:dragonball:Nameless Namekian|single entity]] until he separated the evil from his body. Here, however, the Japanese description's wording suggests that Ganglion came about when Ensanglion separated the good from himself, especially since Ensanglion's Japanese name (Shinglion) could be derived from 真 ''shin'' (true)
**Their relationship is also comparable to the Pokémon [[bulbapedia:Reshiram (Pokémon)|Reshiram]] and [[bulbapedia:Zekrom (Pokémon)|Zekrom]], a duo of opposing dragons that resulted from a single dragon splitting itself into three, though the final dragon created from the splitting has no known [[The Battle Cats|Battle Cats]] equivalent.
**Ganglion the Unleashed's Japanese description states that his blasts of light bury those who stand in his way, with the term used for "bury", 葬り去る ''hōmurisaru'', specifically referring to burying something like the past, not in the ground; leaving something to be forgotten. This may explain why Ganglion is regarded as the founder of all [[Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS (Gacha Event)|Dragon Emperors]] rather than Ensanglion.
**The Japanese descriptions of Ganglion and [[Ultima Beast Naala]], another powerful, ancient Behemoth, both use the word 始祖 ''shiso'' (founder or originator; the first person to start something, or the first in a lineage). Ganglion is said to be the founder/originator of all dragons (全てのドラゴンの始祖 ''subete no doragon no shiso''), while Naala is revered as the founder/originator of all beasts (全ての獣の始祖 ''subete no kemono no shiso'').
**The pink glow that Ensanglion's eyes get when attacking contrasts the [[Media:Ganglion promo.jpeg|green glow]] briefly seen in Ganglion's eyes during his attack animation.
**The [[wikipedia:Star of David|Star of David]] behind Ensanglion also appears in Ganglion the Ancient's attack animation, being the power-up circle seen directly before his attack.
**Ganglion the Unleashed's Weaken [[Talents|Talent]] is a possible reference to Ensanglion's ability to Weaken cats.
*[[Raiden (Uber Rare Cat)|God-Emperor Raiden]]'s Behemoth Slayer Ultra Talent. added in the same update as Ensanglion, may imply that Raiden was built specifically to fight Ensanglion in the event of his return.
**Further supporting this is that Raiden, [[Ganglion (Uber Rare Cat)|Ganglion]] and Ensanglion are all described as ancient in [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]].
**Raiden is also described as "The ONLY Hope against ANCIENT CAT DRAGONS" in the [[Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS (Gacha Event)|Lords of Destruction DRAGON EMPERORS]]' poster.
*Ensanglion seems to be associated with the Moon. The tail on his head ends in a crescent, his horns also give his head a crescent shape, and his second stage is [[Moon Dust Area: Final]], where [[Media:Bg202.gif|the Moon is in full view]].
*The characters present across his design and animations appear to be various characters from the [[Wikipedia:Celestial Alphabet|Celestial Alphabet]].
*Although Ensanglion the Calamity and [[Mysterious Calamity]] are both powerful [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] event enemies with "Calamity" in their name, Omni Strike, Weaken and Immune to Freeze, this may be a coincidence, as their Japanese names use different words for "calamity" (Ensanglion's uses 禍 ''ka'', Mystery Calamity's uses 厄災 ''yakusai'').
*He is one of the four non-collab enemies to be a counterpart of an [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare Cat]], the others being [[Possessed Empress]], [[Revolutionary Nobunaga]] and [[Nuclear Dragon King Berius (PC Enemy)|Nuclear Dragon King Berius]].

